    'body'        => <<<'HTML'
<p class="lead">Clients rarely meet you before they hire you. They meet your profile. A professional freelancer profile does the job of a résumé, a sales pitch and a portfolio at once, and it does that job in the 10 to 30 seconds a busy client spends deciding whether to click "Invite" or move on. This guide walks you through every section, with headline examples, a bio formula and a checklist you can work through tonight.</p>

<div class="key-takeaways"><p class="kt-title">Key takeaways</p><ul>
<li>A professional freelancer profile sells outcomes for a specific type of client, not a list of traits.</li>
<li>Your headline and the first two lines of your bio do most of the work, so make them specific.</li>
<li>Three to six well-explained portfolio pieces beat twenty unexplained ones.</li>
<li>Price from your real costs and target income, not from what the cheapest competitor charges.</li>
<li>Treat the profile as a living document and refresh it every quarter.</li>
